# A keeping RECONSIDER while the lock is held clears no conflict mark (validation.cpp:4180-4215),
# so the main blocks the enforcement disconnected stay marked, above the lock's height too
# (validation.cpp:4124-4132). Spork 19 off and on resets the lock (chainlock/handler.cpp:209-222),
# and the marks outlive it: after an ignoring RECONSIDER, which skips a marked block with its data
# (validation.cpp:4190), the held block on the second main block is bad-prevblk-chainlock
# (validation.cpp:4654). The header-only child keeps that block off getchaintips' tips.
extend main 2
fork 0 1 headers hold
fork 0 1 hold
fork 2 1
cl tip#2
invalidate built#0
reconsider built#0
spork off
cl tip#2
spork on
cl tip#2
reconsider built#0 ignore_cl
deliver b2
